# Script name: .env.example
# Original location: frontend/.env.example
# What this script is: Example environment variable file for a frontend project
# What it is used for: Provides example/default environment variables (not secrets) for local development and documentation
# Programming language: Source/configuration format
# Inputs: None (this file is read by build/runtime tooling rather than receiving runtime inputs)
# Outputs: None (defines environment variables consumed at build/runtime)
# Where output is saved or sent: None
# Technologies and services used or interacted with: Vite, frontend application, HTTP API backend
# Downstream scripts/files/processes that consume the output: Frontend build (Vite), application runtime code, modules/components that make API calls
# Risks and safe change note: Changing values affects which backend endpoints the frontend calls; do not commit secrets here. Safe to edit for local development but verify CI/CD and production configs separately.
# created by: Sadeq Obaid

# Defines the base URL the Vite-powered frontend will use to contact the backend API.
# The VITE_ prefix makes this variable available to client-side code via import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE_URL.
# The value below is an example local endpoint (protocol, host, port, and base path) for development.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000/api/v1
